# Target C-II — unconstrained metric root is outside the H5 order type

**Date:** 2026-09-18  
**Status:** exploratory numerical regression; not a theorem  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_support6_h5_metric_unconstrained_survivor_regression_2026_09_18.py`

The full signed unit-force equations for the tenth simple-wall sign pattern (W9)
have a floating-point root with infinity-norm residual below `2e-14` and minimum
pair distance above `0.2`.  The same point has six convex-hull vertices and the
purported wall triple `036` has nonzero oriented area, so it is not a realization
of the prescribed H5 simple-wall order type.

This is a useful scope regression.  The metric equations alone do not exclude the
W9 signing; the order-type, wall, and source-derived constraints are essential.  It
also confirms that “a numerical solver found no H5 root” would not be a theorem:
unconstrained solves can converge to a different order type.

The result is intentionally not used to weaken the existing exact projection-
potential exclusions of the six uniform and ten simple-wall H5 cases.  It supplies
no global source realization and no C-II closure.

**Classification:** unreviewed candidate/regression, floating-point only.
